\description{
The \code{either} join of a plan: two or more plans run at once, where a fill on one acts on the others.

With the sibling rule \code{cancel}, the first child to fill cancels the others, which is one-cancels-other between whole plans. With \code{reduce}, the children share one quantity and each is kept at that quantity less what its siblings have filled, which is how a stop and a target protect one position; each child must then be a single \code{OrderPart}.
